# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF.
# cmd.exe seeks through a .cmd by byte offset assuming CRLF line endings. With
# bare LF the offset drifts, cmd re-executes fragments of earlier lines, and
# multi-line if/else blocks run BOTH branches. Symptom seen 2026-09-13:
# Approve-SITL.cmd printed "FAILED" and "Done." together, followed by
# 'errorlevel' is not recognized as an internal or external command.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Deliberately NOT setting a repo-wide `* text=auto`: this vault is thousands of
# Obsidian notes, and turning it on would renormalise every one of them into a
# single enormous diff. Only the files cmd.exe parses need pinning.
